{"authored" [{"question" "q-79739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{x}^{3}y-{y}^{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2x+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2x+3{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}x+(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}l$ for the slant height $l$ of the right cone if its base radius is $r=3$ and height $h=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The slant height of the right cone is $l=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}l(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂l}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂l}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=3$  and $h=4$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(3,4) & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a sector of a circle, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ if the radius is $r=4$ and the central angle is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the sector is $S=\\frac{\\theta }{2}{r}^{2}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(r,\\theta ) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂S}{∂\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =r\\theta \\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=xy+x{e}^{y},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(2,0)$ to $(1,-0.5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(y+{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}x+(x+x{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,0) & =(0+{e}^{0})\\,\\text{d}x+(2+2\\cdot {e}^{0})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+4\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+4\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,0)$ to $(1,-0.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-2=-1, \\\\ Δy & =-0.5-0=-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+4\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-0.5) \\\\  & ≈-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ decreases by approximately $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f