s" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+\\sqrt{y},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(0,4)$ to $(-1,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2xy\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,4),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(0,4) & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x+({0}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,4+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(0,4)$ to $(-1,5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =-1-0=-1, \\\\ Δy & =5-4=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $0.25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262dfa728649c57f489" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9da65973e7e0817624f392cc1c48c18427d3da80f1ceeeeab25e63d33dcd83f2" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/state.json" "file_sha256" "193557bbfafc1629a1c5c39dc4092620f9e1d06091b30262df