8/example-6852.json" "file_sha256" "8f4eaebc4cefa1e364a0614d88b75fe4a71ad98ef12a8bd09273bf4c44c28a32" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6852.json" "file_sha256" "8f4eaebc4cefa1e364a0614d88b75fe4a71ad98ef12a8bd09273bf4c44c28a32" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6854.json" "file_sha256" "e3472bb45ef822d35a054ec8b4b5e1a02cbd63d184ffe41d78afc32a09d60467" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the cone is $V = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3) & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi \\cdot 6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =12\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6854.json" "file_sha256" "e3472bb45ef822d35a054ec8b4b5e1a02cbd63d184ffe41d78afc32a09d60467" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f (x, y) = xe^y ,$ use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6875.json" "file_sha256" "d28f9ddbbb5ccdbe634b248c7433d02541277fff3bcbe16b9d18802e1968eb29" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(5,0) & ={e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x+5{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+5\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-5=-3, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+5\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6875.json" "file_sha256" "d28f9ddbbb5ccdbe634b248c7433d02541277fff3bcbe16b9d18802e1968eb29" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6876.json" "file_sha256" "3afaf863ff89565d3ad90a89a700970d12a90e615a7a7403c5a4c09c4fc11865" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx  -1  \\,  \\Delta x + 0  \\,  \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3-\\pi ≈-0.141, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈-1(-0.141)+0(0.2) \\\\  & ≈0.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,0.2) & ≈f(\\pi ,0)+0.141 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0.141 \\\\  & ≈0+1+0.141 \\\\  & ≈1.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/example-6876.json" "file_sha256" "3afaf863ff89565d3ad90a89a700970d12a90e615a7a7403c5a4c09c4fc11865" "basis" 1911 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14059898/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ of the rectangular solid if the base is a square with the side of $a=3$ and the height is $h=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "490631e9caae6aff35de462ff8f0e18814519090b9886a5251afc49e65b0424e" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The surface area of the given rectangular solid is $S=2{a}^{2}+4ah.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =(4a+4h)\\,\\text{d}a+4a\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=3$ and $h=7,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(3,7) & =(4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 7)\\,\\text{d}a+4\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "490631e9caae6aff35de462ff8f0e18814519090b9886a5251afc49e65b0424e" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64ebbe4c5c3339e384772d524cb74d16e51e6558d9210f91128095b076ca4c95" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "490631e9caae6aff35de462ff8f0e18814519090b9886a5251afc49e65b0424e" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "