/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(yz)\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(yz)\\,\\text{d}y+{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(yz)\\,\\text{d}z"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{-y}+y{e}^{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{e}^{-y}]\\,\\text{d}x+[-x{e}^{-y}+{e}^{z}]\\,\\text{d}y+[y{e}^{z}]\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}x+({e}^{z}-x{e}^{-y})\\,\\text{d}y+y{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-167153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}x+(y{e}^{z}+x{e}^{-y})\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "x{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}x+(y{e}^{z}-x{e}^{-y})\\,\\text{d}y+y\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}x+({e}^{z}-x{e}^{-y})\\,\\text{d}y+y{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}y+y{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x-x{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}x+({e}^{z}-x{e}^{-y})\\,\\text{d}y+y{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ of the rectangular solid if the base is a square with the side of $a=3$ and the height is $h=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The surface area of the given rectangular solid is $S=2{a}^{2}+4ah.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =(4a+4h)\\,\\text{d}a+4a\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=3$ and $h=7,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(3,7) & =(4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 7)\\,\\text{d}a+4\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "17\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "20\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "40\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}h"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a sector of a circle, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ if the radius is $r=4$ and the central angle is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the sector is $S=\\frac{\\theta }{2}{r}^{2}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(r,\\theta ) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂S}{∂\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =r\\theta \\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-37295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}r+8\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}l$ for the slant height $l$ of the right cone if its base radius is $r=3$ and height $h=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The slant height of the right cone is $l=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}l(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂l}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂l}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{h}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=3$  and $h=4$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(3,4) & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\,\\text{d}r+4\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangle, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the area $S$ if the lengths of sides are $a=4$ and $b=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the rectangle is $S=ab.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,b) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b \\\\  & =b\\,\\text{d}a+a\\,\\text{d}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=4$ and $b=5,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,5) & =5\\,\\text{d}a+4\\,\\text{d}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{d}a+8\\,\\text{d}b"] ["math" "2\\,\\text{d}a+\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{d}b"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{d}a+5\\,\\text{d}b"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{d}a+4\\,\\text{d}b"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{d}a+2\\,\\text{d}b"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\,\\text{d}a+4\\,\\text{d}b"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=6,$ $b=3,$ and $c=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the rectangular solid is $V=abc.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =bc\\,\\text{d}a+ac\\,\\text{d}b+ab\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=6,$ $b=3,$ and $c=8,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3,8) & =3\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}a+6\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}b+6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "18\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}b+48\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "36\\,\\text{d}a+9\\,\\text{d}b+64\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{d}a+3\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+\\sqrt{y},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(0,4)$ to $(-1,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2xy\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,4),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(0,4) & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x+({0}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,4+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(0,4)$ to $(-1,5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =-1-0=-1, \\\\ Δy & =5-4=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈0\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $0.25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.25"] ["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "0.25"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1.25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.25"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(0,e)$ to $(1,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,e),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(0,e) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡e\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{0}{e}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,e+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+0\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(0,e)$ to $(1,2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-0=1, \\\\ Δy & =2-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+0\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (1)+0\\cdot (2-e) \\\\  & ≈1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2-e"] ["math" "e"] ["math" "e-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=xy+x{e}^{y},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(2,0)$ to $(1,-0.5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(y+{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}x+(x+x{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,0) & =(0+{e}^{0})\\,\\text{d}x+(2+2\\cdot {e}^{0})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+4\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+4\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,0)$ to $(1,-0.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-2=-1, \\\\ Δy & =-0.5-0=-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+4\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-0.5) \\\\  & ≈-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ decreases by approximately $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y,z)=(2x+{y}^{2}-z)^{2},$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(1,2,0)$ to $(2,1.5,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =4(2x+{y}^{2}-z)\\,\\text{d}x+4y(2x+{y}^{2}-z)\\,\\text{d}y-2(2x+{y}^{2}-z)\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,2,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(1,2,0) & =4(2\\cdot 1+{2}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}x+(4\\cdot 2)(2\\cdot 1+{2}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y-2(2\\cdot 1+{2}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{d}x+48\\,\\text{d}y-12\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,2+Δy,0+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈24\\,Δx+48\\,Δy-12\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(1,2,0)$ to $(2,1.5,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-1=1, \\\\ Δy & =1.5-2=-0.5 \\\\ Δz & =1-0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈24\\,Δx+48\\,Δy-12\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈24\\cdot 1+48\\cdot (-0.5)-12\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ≈-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ decreases by approximately $-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-86716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-24"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(1.5,1.5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+0\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(1.5,1.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1.5-2=-0.5, \\\\ Δy & =1.5-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+0\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-0.5)+0\\cdot (1.5-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ≈-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ decreases by approximately $0.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.1"] ["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "-1"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sqrt{4.1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.9)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{4}\\,Δx+1\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4.1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.9)=f(4.1,0.9),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(4.1,0.9).$\n\nMoving from $(4,1)$ to $(4.1,0.9),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =4.1-4=0.1, \\\\ Δy & =0.9-1=-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (0.1)+1(-0.1) \\\\  & ≈0.025-0.1 \\\\  & ≈-0.075.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.075.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4.1,0.9) & ≈f(4,1)-0.075 \\\\ \\sqrt{4.1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.9) & ≈\\sqrt{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-0.075 \\\\  & ≈2-0.075 \\\\  & ≈1.925.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.910"] ["math" "1.915"] ["math" "1.920"] ["math" "1.925"] ["math" "1.930"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.925"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $2.1{e}^{0.2}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$ at the point $(2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & ={e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\cdot {e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n2.1{e}^{0.2}=f(2.1,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(2.1,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $(2,0)$ to $(2.1,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2.1-2=0.1, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\cdot (0.1)+2\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & ≈0.1+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.5.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.1,0.2) & ≈f(2,0)+0.5 \\\\ 2.1{e}^{0.2} & ≈2{e}^{0}+0.5 \\\\  & ≈2+0.5 \\\\  & ≈2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2.1"] ["math" "2.3"] ["math" "2.5"] ["math" "2.7"] ["math" "2.8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate the value of ${e}^{\\sqrt{10}-3.2}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{x}-y}$ at the point $(9,3).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x}-y}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{\\sqrt{x}-y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(9,3),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{9}-3}}{2\\sqrt{9}}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{\\sqrt{9}-3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x-{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x-1\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(9+Δx,3+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{6}\\,Δx-1\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n{e}^{\\sqrt{10}-3.2}=f(10,3.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(10,3.2).$\n\nMoving from $(9,3)$ to $(10,3.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =10-9=1, \\\\ Δy & =3.2-3=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & ≈0.167-0.2 \\\\  & ≈-0.033.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $0.033.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(10,3.2) & ≈f(9,3)-0.033 \\\\ {e}^{\\sqrt{10}-3.2} & ≈{e}^{\\sqrt{9}-3}-0.033 \\\\  & ≈1-0.033 \\\\  & ≈0.967.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-79839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.961"] ["math" "0.965"] ["math" "0.967"] ["math" "0.970"] ["math" "0.972"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-79839" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.967"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)$ at the point $({\\pi }^{2},0).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $({\\pi }^{2},0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x-\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $({\\pi }^{2}+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,Δx-\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2)=f({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $({\\pi }^{2},0)$ to $({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =({\\pi }^{2}+1)-{\\pi }^{2}=1, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈(-\\frac{1}{2\\pi })\\cdot (1)-1\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }-0.2 \\\\  & ≈-0.359.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $-0.359.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2) & ≈f({\\pi }^{2},0)-0.359 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}+0)-0.359 \\\\  & =0-0.359 \\\\  & =-0.359.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.274"] ["math" "-0.359"] ["math" "-0.482"] ["math" "-0.521"] ["math" "-0.652"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-167171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.359"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate ${e}^{(0.3)(2.15)}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}$ at the point $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0,2),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =2\\cdot {e}^{0\\cdot 2}\\,\\text{d}x+0\\cdot {e}^{0\\cdot 2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0+Δx,2+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈2\\,Δx+0\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n{e}^{(0.3)(2.15)}=f(0.3,2.15),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(0.3,2.15).$\n\nMoving from $(0,2)$ to $(0.3,2.15),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =0.3-0=0.3, \\\\ Δy & =2.15-2=0.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈2\\cdot (0.3)+0\\cdot (0.15) \\\\  & ≈0.6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.6.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.3,2.15) & ≈f(0,2)+0.6 \\\\ {e}^{(0.3)(2.15)} & ≈{e}^{(0)(2)}+0.6 \\\\  & ≈1+0.6 \\\\  & ≈1.6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "881e5874e07ad3e6df6c7cdd1a13c6a42734a08a0d1563c34a3951bbf1389aae"} {"question" "q-86717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.6"] ["math" "-1.6"] ["math" "-2.6"] ["math" "0.6"] ["math" "1.6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "q-86717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af1851ff8675258091660e791d82a5f42ca28beaefd7982cd290356b83c0571"} {"question" "e-6852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the differential for $f(x,y) = x^2 \\sin y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6852.json" "file_sha256" "8f4eaebc4cefa1e364a0614d88b75fe4a71ad98ef12a8bd09273bf4c44c28a32"} {"question" "e-6852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6852.json" "file_sha256" "8f4eaebc4cefa1e364a0614d88b75fe4a71ad98ef12a8bd09273bf4c44c28a32"} {"question" "e-6854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6854.json" "file_sha256" "e3472bb45ef822d35a054ec8b4b5e1a02cbd63d184ffe41d78afc32a09d60467"} {"question" "e-6854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the cone is $V = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3) & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi \\cdot 6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =12\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6854.json" "file_sha256" "e3472bb45ef822d35a054ec8b4b5e1a02cbd63d184ffe41d78afc32a09d60467"} {"question" "e-6875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f (x, y) = xe^y ,$ use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6875.json" "file_sha256" "d28f9ddbbb5ccdbe634b248c7433d02541277fff3bcbe16b9d18802e1968eb29"} {"question" "e-6875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(5,0) & ={e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x+5{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+5\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-5=-3, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+5\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6875.json" "file_sha256" "d28f9ddbbb5ccdbe634b248c7433d02541277fff3bcbe16b9d18802e1968eb29"} {"question" "e-6876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6876.json" "file_sha256" "3afaf863ff89565d3ad90a89a700970d12a90e615a7a7403c5a4c09c4fc11865"} {"question" "e-6876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx  -1  \\,  \\Delta x + 0  \\,  \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3-\\pi ≈-0.141, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈-1(-0.141)+0(0.2) \\\\  & ≈0.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,0.2) & ≈f(\\pi ,0)+0.141 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0.141 \\\\  & ≈0+1+0.141 \\\\  & ≈1.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070766/example-6876.json" "file_sha256" "3afaf863ff89565d3ad90a89a700970d12a90e615a7a7403c5a4c09c4fc11865"}] "usage" {"e-6876" [] "q-79958" [] "q-79840" [] "q-167171" [] "q-37282" [] "e-6852" [] "q-79739" [] "q-79813" [] "q-79747" [] "q-37295" [] "e-6875" [] "q-168150" [] "e-6854" [] "q-79810" []} "basis" 2507 "retractions" [[17592186124968 :question/problem "Find the differential $df$ for the function $f(x, y, z) = \\cos (xy) - 2z^{2}y$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186122831 17592186122832 17592186122833 1759218